-- THE CLOSURE RULE SUBSUMES THE CONVOY. A let leaves its unfolding
-- equation in the context (el-let), so a component named by a Σ split
-- sits next to (x1 ≡ x .π₁). That entry MENTIONS x1, hence joins the
-- dependency-closed suffix the moment x1 is eliminated, and the
-- Π-closure carries it into the motive by the ordinary rule — no
-- convoy case, no second motive discipline. The entry is ANONYMOUS,
-- so it is re-applied as ⋆: proofs are irrelevant, and the ambient
-- inhabitant discharges it.
def P : ℕ → 𝕌 ≔ λn. ℕ

def c : (x : ℕ × ℕ) → P (x .π₁) ≔ λx. (let x1 ≔ x .π₁ in
                                       let x2 ≔ x .π₂ in
                                       (?g : (P x1)))
